Author: Tian Shilin <tianshilin@uniontech.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 02 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: Fix '#' prefix in paint server ID lookup causing gradient resolution failure

The fix-resolving-paint-servers-stack-overflow.patch replaced the recursive
resolvePaintServers() implementation with an iterative one, but the new code
calls m_doc->namedStyle(id) directly without stripping the '#' prefix from
the paint style ID. The old code path via structureNode->styleProperty(id)
automatically stripped the '#' prefix via QSvgNode::styleProperty(const QString &).

This caused all gradient and pattern references in SVGs to fail resolution,
resulting in fills being set to Qt::NoBrush (transparent).

Observed with the Tencent Meeting SVG icon (wemeet.svg) which uses four
linearGradient references via url(#paintN_linear_...).

Bug: QTBUG-145916

Index: qt6-svg/src/svg/qsvghandler.cpp
===================================================================
--- qt6-svg.orig/src/svg/qsvghandler.cpp
+++ qt6-svg/src/svg/qsvghandler.cpp
@@ -4904,6 +4904,8 @@ void QSvgHandler::resolvePaintServers()
         if (prop->type() == QSvgStyleProperty::FILL) {
             QSvgFillStyle *fill = static_cast<QSvgFillStyle *>(prop);
             QString id = fill->paintStyleId();
+            if (id.startsWith(QLatin1Char('#')))
+                id.remove(0, 1);
             QSvgPaintStyleProperty *style = m_doc->namedStyle(id);
             if (style) {
                 fill->setFillStyle(style);
@@ -4914,6 +4916,8 @@ void QSvgHandler::resolvePaintServers()
         } else if (prop->type() == QSvgStyleProperty::STROKE) {
             QSvgStrokeStyle *stroke = static_cast<QSvgStrokeStyle *>(prop);
             QString id = stroke->paintStyleId();
+            if (id.startsWith(QLatin1Char('#')))
+                id.remove(0, 1);
             QSvgPaintStyleProperty *style = m_doc->namedStyle(id);
             if (style) {
                 stroke->setStyle(style);
